/-!
# Every `E677` magma with seven elements has an idempotent

If `op : Fin 7 → Fin 7 → Fin 7` satisfies `x = op y (op x (op (op y x) y))` for all `x y`, then
`op x x = x` for some `x`.

## Proof

By contradiction: `E677Idem7.H op` is equation 677 together with `op x x ≠ x` for every `x`,
and `E677Idem7.root : H op → False` is a case split on the cells of the table.

* After each decision the rules `r1`, `r3`, `r4` (one instance of equation 677 together with
  the injectivity of a row, `H.inj`) and `rcK` (the last open cell of a row) derive cells; a
  derived cell is one line `have cYC := r1 h ...`.  A branch closes by `k1` (equation 677 gives a
  different value), `kr` (two equal values in one row) or `h.ni` (an idempotent).
* The branched cell is the open cell with the fewest surviving values (first fail).  `cvK`
  splits on the seven values of a cell.
* Symmetry: when two values `v₀ < v` of the branched cell are labels that neither a decision on
  the path nor the row or column of the branched cell mentions, the branch `v` is the branch
  `v₀` for the relabelled operation
  `conj op (Equiv.swap v₀ v)` (`H.cj`, `cc`); the branch `v₀` is a lemma `symK`.
* Subtrees of more than 300 lines are lemmas `nK`.

The search has 1981 nodes.  The finite fact is prior work (ETP Zulip: D. McNeil, 2024-12-07;
J. Brox, 2025-03-26, the two isomorphism classes of order 7; B. Reinke, 2026-05-15;
S. Chuks-Onah, 2026-05-16).  The declarations of the namespace `E677Idem7` were generated by
`experiments/analysis/small-order-lean-2026-10-26/gen_idem.py` (options `--n 7 --noidem`)
of a private repo (Adam McKenna), from the branching choices of its counter
`count_dfs 7 --noidem --heur ff`.
-/

open FiniteMagmaE677

namespace E677Idem7

/-- An operation on `Fin 7`. -/
abbrev Op := Fin 7 → Fin 7 → Fin 7

/-- The hypotheses of the case split. -/
structure H (op : Op) : Prop where
  /-- Equation 677. -/
  e : ∀ x y : Fin 7, x = op y (op x (op (op y x) y))
  /-- No element is idempotent. -/
  ni : ∀ x : Fin 7, op x x ≠ x

/-- Each row of an E677 operation is injective. -/
theorem H.inj {op : Op} (h : H op) (y : Fin 7) : Function.Injective (op y) :=
  Finite.injective_iff_surjective.mpr fun x => ⟨_, (h.e x y).symm⟩

/-- Every element of `Fin 7` is a numeral; the value `0` is the last case. -/
theorem cv0 (w : Fin 7) : w = 1 ∨ w = 2 ∨ w = 3 ∨ w = 4 ∨ w = 5 ∨ w = 6 ∨ w = 0 := by
  revert w
  decide

/-- Every element of `Fin 7` is a numeral; the value `1` is the last case. -/
theorem cv1 (w : Fin 7) : w = 0 ∨ w = 2 ∨ w = 3 ∨ w = 4 ∨ w = 5 ∨ w = 6 ∨ w = 1 := by
  revert w
  decide

/-- Every element of `Fin 7` is a numeral; the value `2` is the last case. -/
theorem cv2 (w : Fin 7) : w = 0 ∨ w = 1 ∨ w = 3 ∨ w = 4 ∨ w = 5 ∨ w = 6 ∨ w = 2 := by
  revert w
  decide

/-- Every element of `Fin 7` is a numeral; the value `3` is the last case. -/
theorem cv3 (w : Fin 7) : w = 0 ∨ w = 1 ∨ w = 2 ∨ w = 4 ∨ w = 5 ∨ w = 6 ∨ w = 3 := by
